{"created": "2026-03-25T15:17:19.433565+00:00", "modified": "2026-03-25T15:17:19.744913+00:00", "id": 19222374, "conceptrecid": "17671959", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19222374", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.17671959", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19222374", "metadata": {"title": "MS-Net: Multi-Similarity based network annotation for untargeted metabolomics: Raw LC-MS data and processing outputs from Cannabis extract", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19222374", "publication_date": "2026-03-25", "description": "<p>Raw LC-MS data in POS and NEG mode acquired from <em>Cannabis</em> extracts. Outputs from MZmine processing and&nbsp;<em>in silico</em> annotation (Sirius) are also available and ready for MS-Net.</p>\n<p>Acquisition method:</p>\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Chromatographic separation was carried out on a Vanquish UHPLC system (Thermo Fisher Scientific, Waltham, MA, USA) equipped with a Luna Omega Polar C18 analytical column (150 &times; 2.1 mm, 1.6 &micro;m; Phenomenex, Torrance, CA, USA). The chromatographic system was coupled with a Vanquish Diode Array Detector (DAD), a Charged Aerosol Detector (CAD) and a Q-exactive Plus mass spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific, Waltham, MA, USA). A dual-pump system was installed, where the first pump managed the separation at the column Level, and the second pump system generated a counter-gradient at the column outlet to maintain a constant mixture of 50% water and 50% acetonitrile. The separation was performed at a flow rate of 0.4 mL&middot;min</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">\u207b</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&sup1; and at a column oven temperature of 40 &deg;C, using a mobile phase composed of H</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">\u2082</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">O + 0.05% formic acid (A) and acetonitrile + 0.05% formic acid (B). A 1 &micro;L injection of extracts at 10 mg&middot;mL</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">\u207b</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&sup1; was introduced into the system. The applied gradient was as follows: 0 to 0.5 min, 2% B; 0.5 to 18 min, 98% B; 18 to 21 min, 98% B; 21 to 21.5 min, 2% B; and 21.4 to 24 min, 2% B.</span></p>\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Mass spectrometry detection was performed using a Q Exactive Plus instrument equipped with a heated electrospray ionization source (HESI-II) operating in positive and negative ionization modes with a resolution of 35,000 (MS1) and 17,500 (MS2). The collision energy was set to 10, 20, and 40 eV in stepped mode for data-dependent MS/MS acquisition. The capillary temperature was 300&deg;C, and the mass scan range was 100&ndash;1,500 m/z for both MS1 and MS2. Data-dependent acquisition targeted the four most intense precursor ions per scan cycle.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Marti, Guillaume", "affiliation": "Universit\u00e9 de Toulouse", "orcid": "0000-0002-6321-9005"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Marti, Guillaume", "affiliation": "Universit\u00e9 de Toulouse", "type": "DataManager", "orcid": "0000-0002-6321-9005"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://zenodo.org/records/17669288", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.21203/rs.3.rs-8174529/v1", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication", "scheme": "doi"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "agromix"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "17671959"}}]}}, "title": "MS-Net: Multi-Similarity based network annotation for untargeted metabolomics: Raw LC-MS data and processing outputs from Cannabis extract", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19222374", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19222374?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19222374", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19222374", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.19222374", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/17671959", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/17671959", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17671959", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.17671959", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19222374/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19222374/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19222374/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19222374/requests"}, "updated": "2026-03-25T15:17:19.744913+00:00", "recid": "19222374", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "2c18cbb8-5